      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this will always be the last index in the chain.\n\n- If you\u0027re storing a whole column, you have an `access` that produces a pointer to a vector, so it\u0027ll be the last index that gives you that.\n- If you\u0027re storing a vector element in a dynamically indexed matrix column, the `access` will also be producing a vector and it\u0027ll be the last index.\n\nSo I don\u0027t think you need to do the `FlattenAccessChain` stuff here - we only need to look at at most one `access` instruction. You\u0027ll still need to loop through the types to get the matrix type unfortunately, but I think there\u0027s still a simplification to be made here.",
